    "judgment": {
      "status": "source_error",
      "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions and are mathematically correct. The source error is in q-73608's derivation: the determinant of [[1,1],[1,k]] is k-1, whereas MA writes 1-k. Both are nonzero when k≠1, so this error does not change the correct selected answer. q-73565: det(A)=12-12=0; the two lines coincide, and the inverse does not exist, so I and III hold. q-47652: det(A)=5(k-1)≠0; Ax=0 has the unique zero solution, and the two inhomogeneous lines intersect once, so I and III hold. q-31919: a nonzero determinant means invertible, so only I holds. q-73608: subtracting the two homogeneous equations gives (k-1)y=0, hence y=x=0. q-128144: f′(1)=(2,1,1) and g′(1)=(1,3,0), giving (0,-5,1). The source's notation (f(1)-2g(1))′ is imprecise; the intended quantity is the derivative evaluated at t=1. q-127998: componentwise differentiation gives (-1,2t-2,3t²+2t-2). q-71233: the product rule gives e^t(f+f′), yielding the selected vector. q-70688: differentiating (2sin²t,sin t cos t,e^t sin t) gives (2sin(2t),cos(2t),e^t(cos t+sin t)). q-70695: the composition is (cos(e^t),e^(3t),t), whose derivative is the selected vector. q-128561: the composition is -t i+e^(-2t) j+e^(-t/2) k, giving the selected derivative. q-32347: f×g=(-10t²-2t,18-24t³+6t²,18t⁴-6t), so its derivative is (-20t-2,-72t²+12t,72t³-6). q-32353: f×g=(21t²+20t,8t+16-15t³,-6t⁴-t²-6t-8), giving (42t+20,8-45t²,-24t³-2t-6). q-142562: summing the Y=2 column gives 0.25+0.05+0.15=0.45. q-142559: summing the Y=1 column gives 1/4+1/8=3/8. q-142826: the Y column sums are 0.45 and 0.55. q-142833: the X row sums are 0.55, 0.15, and 0.3. Every MA answer below is supported by a contiguous verbatim span of that question's worked solution; no grade evidence was supplied.",
